nt-of-accounts-2025-26-approval-of-acc.pdf","committee":"Governance & Standards Committee","date":"25/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"Extract Minute - G & S Investment Strategies","url":"https://Mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s8146/extract-minute-g-s-investment-strategies.pdf","committee":"Council","date":"03/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendices for Investment Strategies~1","url":"https://Mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s8148/appendices-for-investment-strategies-1.pdf","committee":"Council","date":"03/03/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-26","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Place)","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-06","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Communities & Services)","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Audit, Governance & Standards Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Place)","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Communities & Services)","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-10","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Corporate Resources)","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-17","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Corporate Resources)","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-18","committee":"Audit, Governance & Standards Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Communities & Services)","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Corporate Resources)","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Council Acting as Charity Trustees","time":"6.45 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Audit, Governance & Standards Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Mansfield Council defers \u00a333.8m capital investment as digital programme stalls","lead":"Mansfield Council has generated a \u00a3169,000 surplus on day-to-day spending at the end of the first quarter, but is deferring over a third of its planned capital investment \u2014 money spent on long-lived assets such as buildings and equipment \u2014 to next year. The council is carrying forward \u00a326.8m of General Fund capital and \u00a37m of Housing Revenue Account capital to 2027/28. The biggest delay is the Mansfield Connect digital transformation programme, budgeted at \u00a323.7m for this year but now forecast to spend only \u00a31m. The White Hart Street housing development, a new-build scheme for council tenants, is 75 per cent underspent and will not start as planned. The slippage suggests the council is struggling to deliver major investment projects, though it has avoided an overall budget overspend partly because it is earning \u00a3300,000 more in interest on its investments than it budgeted.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Decision notice","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9980/9980.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Mansfield Council reports modest surplus as capital programme slips by \u00a334m","lead":"Mansfield Council has generated a \u00a3169,000 revenue surplus\u2014day-to-day spending\u2014in the first quarter of 2026/27, transferred to reserves as its running budget stays broadly on track. However, the council is deferring \u00a333.8m of capital investment, money spent on long-lived assets, to next year, including a 98 per cent underspend on its flagship Mansfield Connect digital transformation programme, which has delivered only \u00a3459,833 of a \u00a323.7m budget. A separate housing development at White Hart Street is 75 per cent underspent and has not begun as planned. The slippage has eliminated the council's borrowing requirement for the year, reducing the amount it must set aside to repay past borrowing by \u00a3139,000. The council is meanwhile facing recruitment pressures: at least 15 service areas report they cannot hold posts vacant to meet savings targets, and budgeted savings of \u00a3187,000 are now forecast to deliver only \u00a3112,000. A \u00a3500,000 shortfall in housing rents reflects void properties\u2014empty dwellings\u2014rising to 6.1 per cent from a budgeted 2.75 per cent, though higher investment income of \u00a3300,000 has offset some pressures.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Decision notice","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9980/9980.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Mansfield Council borrows \u00a315m in quarter with half its debt due within a year","lead":"Mansfield Council borrowed \u00a315m in the first three months of 2026/27 and expects to raise \u00a350m more this year, taking total debt toward \u00a3135m. Nearly half its existing borrowing\u2014\u00a346.8m of \u00a398.8m\u2014matures within 12 months, forcing the council to refinance at short notice. The council is betting that interest rates will fall to limit refinancing costs, but early repayment charges on its \u00a352.7m Public Works Loan Board debt are so expensive that it cannot reschedule loans if rates hold steady or rise. Treasury management papers show investment income is running \u00a3300,000 above budget because base rates remained at 3.75% longer than forecast, but this benefit is temporary and will reverse if rates fall as expected.","iso":"2026-09-23","paper_title":"Statement of Accounts 2025/26 - Pension Assumptions","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9920/9920.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"MTFP Update","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9984/9984.pdf","headline":"Capital programme carrying forward \u00a333.798m (32% of approved budget) to 2027/28 due to slippage.","detail":"The capital programme shows significant slippage, with \u00a326.780m of General Fund capital and \u00a37.018m of HRA capital (totalling \u00a333.798m) forecast to be carried forward to 2027/28, representing approximately 32% of the approved \u00a3106.398m budget. The paper notes the slippage has affected both General Fund and HRA but does not explain its causes.","category":"capital","matters":"Substantial capital slippage may indicate underlying delivery challenges such as procurement delays, planning issues, or contractor availability problems that could persist into future years.","figures":"\u00a326.780m GF carry-forward, \u00a37.018m HRA carry-forward, \u00a3106.398m approved budget","quote":"There has been slippage in the capital programme, which has affected both the General Fund and Housing Revenue Account.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"MTFP Update","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9984/9984.pdf","headline":"Section 24 Direction from Local Government Reorganisation will restrict Mansfield's financial autonomy from late 2026.","detail":"Local Government Reorganisation is proceeding with Option 1Bii selected as the preferred structure. When the Structural Changes Order is published towards the end of 2026, the Secretary of State will issue a Section 24 Direction that will prevent the council from making significant financial commitments without the consent of the incoming shadow authority. The council explicitly states this will directly impact its financial decisions.","category":"governance","matters":"Restrictions on financial autonomy create uncertainty around the council's ability to make borrowing decisions, capital commitments, or respond to emerging financial pressures independently.","figures":"None","quote":"At the same time, the Secretary of State will also issue a Section 24 Direction, which will prevent outgoing predecessor councils from making significant financial commitments without the consent of the incoming shadow authority. This will directly impact the financial decisions that Mansfield District Council can take.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"MTFP Update","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9984/9984.pdf","headline":"Mansfield forecasts \u00a33.151m deficit in 2027/28 to be covered by reserve drawdown.","detail":"The updated medium-term financial plan identifies a deficit of \u00a33.151m in 2027/28, driven by a significant decrease in business rates funding due to the reset of the business rates system. The council plans to use its NNDR (business rates) earmarked reserve to balance this deficit, with the arrangement to be reviewed during the 2027/28 budget-setting process.","category":"reserves","matters":"A deficit covered by reserve drawdown is not sustainable long-term; if the underlying budget problem is not resolved, reserves will deplete and the council will face financial pressure in subsequent years.","figures":"\u00a33.151m deficit forecast for 2027/28","quote":"It is recommended that the NNDR reserve set aside for this purpose is utilised to balance the deficit in 2027/28. This will be reviewed as part of the 2027/28 budget-setting process.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"MTFP Update","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9984/9984.pdf","headline":"General Fund forecast to achieve \u00a31.260m surplus in 2026/27, increasing reserves to \u00a33.385m.","detail":"The council is forecasting a surplus of \u00a31.260m on its 2026/27 revenue budget, which will increase General Fund balances from \u00a32.125m to \u00a33.385m. This surplus is \u00a31.285m above the minimum level of balances approved for the year, providing financial headroom.","category":"reserves","matters":"A strong reserve position improves the council's financial resilience and ability to manage future pressures or unexpected costs.","figures":"\u00a31.260m surplus forecast, opening balance \u00a32.125m, projected closing balance \u00a33.385m, \u00a31.285m above minimum","quote":"At the end of the financial year, the General Fund is forecast to achieve a surplus position against its budget of \u00a31.260m, which will increase the level of General Fund balances available.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Appendix 2","paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9986/9986.pdf","headline":"External Wall Insulation scheme discontinued; \u00a3200k budget reallocated to other housing assistance.","detail":"The council has cancelled its External Wall Insulation programme and reallocated the \u00a3200k budget: \u00a387,265 to Discretionary Assistance and \u00a3112,735 to Healthy Homes Grant. The scheme is noted as 'no longer to be completed'. This represents a policy decision to cease this capital programme and redirect resources.","category":"capital","matters":"Programme cancellations can indicate either policy shifts or practical delivery constraints. Discontinuing an energy efficiency programme may reflect funding pressures, procurement difficulties, or reprioritization, all of which are relevant to understanding the council's capital strategy and financial flexibility.","figures":"EWI budget cancelled \u00a3200,000; reallocated to Discretionary Assistance \u00a387,265; Healthy Homes Grant \u00a3112,735","quote":"EWI not being offered this year budget to be used to fund other assistance","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-24"},"name":"Mansfield","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Capital programme carrying forward \u00a333.798m (32% of approved budget) to 2027/28 due to slippage.","lead":"Substantial capital slippage may indicate underlying delivery challenges such as procurement delays, planning issues, or contractor availability problems that could persist into future years.","also":["67 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Place) on 2026-09-26","n_findings":68,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"MTFP Update","top_paper_url":"https://mansfield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s9984/9984.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":142,"news_drafts_total":3}}